  "body": "Standardize 3D `Deburr` on chamfer chord width `w`, add Constant Depth sizing, and support multi-pass edge breaks.\n\n## Where\n\n- `crates/motion/src/finishing3d/deburr.rs` (`DeburrParams`)\n- `crates/motion/tests/deburr.rs` (`deburr_at_the_wall_corner_is_chamfer_byte_for_byte`)\n- `crates/app/src/operation/types/params.rs`, `sane.rs`, `crates/app/src/stock_sim_breaks.rs`\n- `crates/app/src/project/file.rs` (`PROJECT_VERSION`), `crates/app/src/mcp/`, `crates/ui/src/egui_app/`\n\n## What to change\n\n1. Redefine `DeburrParams.width` and `OpParams::Deburr.width` as chamfer chord width `w = 2 * s * sin(theta / 2)` across all wedge angles `theta` (default `0.5 mm`). Keep `Chamfer2D.width` unchanged as its 2D horizontal leg width.\n2. Increment `PROJECT_VERSION` (`61` -> `62`) and multiply legacy 3D `Deburr.width` values by `sqrt(2)` on load (the 90-degree corner ratio). Update `deburr_at_the_wall_corner_is_chamfer_byte_for_byte` to pass `w = 2.0 * sqrt(2)`.\n3. Add `break_mode` (`ConstantWidth` default, `ConstantDepth`), `break_profile` (`Chamfer` default, `Round`), and multi-pass step parameters to `DeburrParams` and `OpParams::Deburr`.\n4. Compute setback `s = d / cos(theta / 2)` for `ConstantDepth`. Emit outer-to-final cone chamfer passes within `EdgeBreak::floor_at`, and refuse `Round` by name on sharp cones until ball-tipped cutters run.\n5. Wire all settings through commands, project files, MCP `ParamsDto`, and UI controls.\n\n## Done means\n\n- Legacy v61 `Deburr` projects migrate cleanly by `sqrt(2)` and keep matching cut depth on 90-degree corners.\n- `ConstantWidth` and `ConstantDepth` cones cut multi-pass bevels that stay inside `EdgeBreak` bounds and pass verify.\n- `Round` on a sharp cone refuses by name, and UI, MCP, and migration tests pass.\n\nPart of #1827\n",
